A||||21||sluppy123||Fiero to Recieve National Recognition||||1||
Z||000000||sluppy123||09-13-1999||10:41 PM||||This is a article that was in the Sept newsletter from the Midwest Fieros, located in Onawa, Iowa<P>"Dennis Gage was at the Pontiac Oakland car show in Council Bluffs, Iowa on Aug 29 to film a segment for his national t.v. show "My Classic car". As he was surveying the Pontiacs deciding which cars he wanted to feature on his show, he noticed our large number of Fieros that were present (sixteen) -(we took home the award for the largest club displaying)-and decided to film one of them for his show. He picked Midwest Fieros member Kenn and his black 88 GT T-top. Kenn was wired with a microphone and answered questions by Mr. Gage while the film crew did their thing. ect..."<P>They couldn't of picked a better car to show. Kenn's is the best example of a 88' GT T-top I have seen. The show should air sometime in early spring. I don't know the date but I will let everybody know when I hear more  <p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 09-14-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-13-1999||11:52 PM||||I watch that show all the time and have seen segments on GT 40s, 427 Cobra (real one), and many other awesome cars. I watch that show waiting for the day I see a Fiero. Anyone ever seen a segment of the Fiero on TV besides Autoweek?<P>BTW, It's called "my Classic Car"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||ChadMan||09-14-1999||09:38 AM||||"My Classic Car" is great.  They had one on Corvairs a couple of weeks ago and I wondered, "Where are the Fieros?"  Now I know - wait and see.<P>SCCA, you mentioned MotorWeek, so I thought I'd plug the MotorWeek "Fiero" tape you can get from the Fiero Store.  It's really good from a historical standpoint and has lots of really cool footage of Fieros at speed. Tests include:<P>1984 SE, in which they think the Fiero is the greatest thing since sliced bread<BR>1985 GT, in which they're impressed by the V6, but are no longer gushing<BR>1986 GT, in which they start badmouthing Fiero handling.  One of their testers loops the Fiero during the slalom test and tries to blame the car, but if you watch the tape, it's clear that he suffers a brain fart and brakes while turning, causing the spin<BR>1988 GT/Formula intro test at Mid-Ohio, in which they again think the Fiero is great - features detailed footage of a yellow GT with power steering!<BR>1988 Formula vs. supercharged MR2 - the Fiero wins!||||reg||14
Z||000003||sluppy123||01-12-2000||05:13 PM||||The show will air Jan. 22,23, Feb. 27, and March 4. Check your local listing for times.<BR>-Brian||||reg||14
