Z||000007||fierosound||01-13-2000||01:44 PM||||When the Fiero first came out ALMOST ALL the national car magazines thought it was the best thing since sliced bread.  Sure, it had a few flaws (like underpowered, needed better suspension etc.), but they were willing to look past these at the revolutionary aspects of the car.  They expected GM would address these problems in future models.  Of course GM didn't "go all out" in all the directions they'd wished fast enough for them.  After that, the flaws were all they could talk about...  See the website below for their early praise...<P> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/stat.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/stat.txt</A> ||||reg||10
